    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1f99a6e7-3577-50ca-b9ca-b4925f6347f1",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-6 & =-2x+6 \\\\ -2x-6+2x & =-2x+6+2x \\\\ -6 & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-9 & =2x-9 \\\\ 3x-9-2x & =2x-9-2x \\\\ x-9 & =-9 \\\\ x-9+9 & =-9+9 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $3x-9=2x-9$ has the unique solution $x=0.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+4 & =2x+2 \\\\ 2x+4-2x & =2x+2-2x \\\\ 4 & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
